70:19&#x02013;27. doi:10.1111/j.1469-8137.1971.tb02504.x </citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Helgason</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Daniell</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Husband</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitter</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ploughing up the wood-wide web?</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1998</year><volume>394</volume><fpage>431</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/28764</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Helgason T, Daniell TJ, Husband R, Fitter AH, Young JP (1998) Ploughing up the wood-wide web? Nature 394:431. doi:10.1038/28764 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9697763</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hijri</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>S&#x000fd;korov&#x000e1;</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Oehl</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Ineichen</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000e4;der</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiemken</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Redecker</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Communities of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi in arable soils are not necessarily low in diversity</article-title><source>Mol Ecol</source><year>2006</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>2277</fpage><lpage>2289</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-294X.2006.02921.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hijri I, S&#x000fd;korov&#x000e1; Z, Oehl F, Ineichen K, M&#x000e4;der P, Wiemken A, Redecker D (2006) Communities of arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi in arable soils are not necessarily low in diversity. Mol Ecol 15:2277&#x02013;2289. doi:10.1111/j.1365-294X.2006.02921.x <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16780440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><citation citation-type="other">IFOAM (2007) The IFOAM basic standards for organic production and processing (available from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.ifoam.org">www.ifoam.org</ext-link>, periodically updated)</citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jansa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mozafar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Anken</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruh</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanders</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Frossard</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diversity and structure of AM communities as affected by tillage in a temperate soil</article-title><source>Mycorrhiza</source><year>2002</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>225</fpage><lpage>234</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00572-002-0163-z</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Jansa J, Mozafar A, Anken T, Ruh R, Sanders IR, Frossard E (2002a) Diversity and structure of AM communities as affected by tillage in a temperate soil. Mycorrhiza 12:225&#x02013;234. doi:10.1007/s00572-002-0163-z <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12375133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jansa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mozafar</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Banke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Frossard</surname><given-name